In the present case, from the facts and submissions referred above, it transpires that young bride has not able to survive her married life for even seven months.
The cause of death has been opined to be 'Asphyxia' due to ante-mortem hanging.
Bail application of co-accused Ramniwas (father-in-law of deceased) has already been rejected by co-ordinate Bench, still there is a substance in the argument of learned counsel for applicant that present applicant is a student who is in jail since 23.12.2021 as well as that the nature of allegations appears to be omnibus and similar to all the accused persons.
There is no specific allegation against applicant and on the basis of similar evidence one of co-accused has been exonerated, therefore, applicant may also entitle for benefit of proviso to Section 437 Cr.P.C. and, therefore, she has made out a case for bail.
